// Policy 5 of 7 -- "Human approval for large trades", from the AWS AgentCore temporal-policies
// article.
//
// THE ARTICLE'S STATED INTENT, verbatim:
//   "Any individual trade over $25,000 requires advisor approval, one approval per trade."
//
// Transcribed as published, with the `eventResource: resource` joins dropped as everywhere else
// in this directory.
//
// THE ONLY POLICY OF THE SEVEN THAT USES `since`, and it is the operator that makes "one approval
// per trade" statable: an approval counts only while no trade has consumed it. `!(A) since within
// W B` is standard past-time MFOTL Since with a negated left operand -- B held inside the window,
// and A has held at NO point after it.
//
// It is also the only one that puts a Cedar comparison and a temporal block on either side of a
// `||`, which is how "under $25,000, or approved" is written as one condition.
permit (
    principal,
    action == AgentCore::Action::"execute_trade",
    resource
)
when {
    context.input.cost < 25000 || temporal {
        !(
            AgentCore::Action::"execute_trade"::response{ }
        )
        since within 24h (
            AgentCore::Action::"approve_trade"::response{ input.status: "approved" }
        )
    }
};
